===Etymology===
Compound of {{compound|säugen|Tier|t1=suckle, give suck|t2=animal|lang=de}}. ''Säuge-'' (from {{m|de|säugen||to suckle}} is part of the compound ''Säugetier'' ("suckling animal") because female mammals nurse their young with milk, which is secreted from special glands, the mammary glands.

